<title>UK: NWE oil products steady, naphtha eases.</title>
<headline>NWE oil products steady, naphtha eases.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE oil products were steady on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Gasoline was steady. Regular barges traded at $199 fob ARA.</p>
<p>Naphtha was easier as a trade at $216 cif Antwerp for 71 paraffinic material was digested by the market.</p>
<p>Gas oil barge premiums were up to $1, but outright prices held steady because of stronger IPE futures.</p>
<p>High and low sulphur fuel oil were steady.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
</text>
